WEBVTT

00:03:28.704 --> 00:03:31.371
pretty much anyone would lend
someone their umbrella,

00:03:31.413 --> 00:03:34.996
but the way this guy acted
at the football game,

00:03:35.038 --> 00:03:36.871
that was unusual."

00:03:36.913 --> 00:03:40.371
And so, you decide to go
with your first impression.

00:03:40.413 --> 00:03:42.329
There's a good moral in this data:

00:03:42.371 --> 00:03:45.371
your brain, and by extension you,
might care more

00:03:45.413 --> 00:03:48.663
about the very negative, immoral
things another person has done

00:03:48.704 --> 00:03:51.204
compared to the very
positive, moral things,

00:03:51.246 --> 00:03:52.913
but it's a direct result

00:03:52.954 --> 00:03:56.329
of the comparative rarity 
of those bad behaviors.

00:03:56.371 --> 00:03:58.704
We’re more used to people 
being basically good,

00:03:58.746 --> 00:04:01.121
like taking time to help
a stranger in need.